NusaShell Telegram plugin

This plugin uses the following open-source components:

- [mymmrac/telego](https://github.com/mymmrac/telego) — Telegram Bot API
  client library (MIT). Production-tested on GoClaw multi-tenant
  deployments.
- [mark3labs/mcp-go](https://github.com/mark3labs/mcp-go) — MCP SDK
  for Go (MIT). Also used by the NusaShell Kanban plugin.
- [NusaShell](https://github.com/jahrulnr/NusaShell) — the shell
  runtime and mcpkit helpers.

Pattern references (not copied):

- GoClaw (nlb_io / nlb_io) — pairing via native Telegram message,
  album coalescing, streaming preview via editMessageText, default-deny
  ACL. See `telegram-research/06-ui-ux-from-real-code.md`.
- OpenClaw (Peter Steinberger) — inline button approval flow,
  session per chat/group/topic.
- Hermes Agent (NousResearch) — multi-platform adapter patterns.

GoClaw is an external project (CC BY-NC 4.0). Its patterns are
referenced for research purposes only.
